---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="How Much Extra Quilt Batting Do You Need?"
  guideSlug="how-much-extra-batting"
  guideCategory="reference"
  description="Plan batting overage around a quilt top and check whether the required rectangle fits a roll or precut width."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Batting extends beyond every edge</h2><p>
      Add the chosen overage twice to width and twice to length. Four inches per
      side turns a 60 × 80 inch top into a 68 × 88 inch batting requirement.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Overage varies by setup</h2><p>
      The 4-inch default is longarm-oriented and editable. Domestic-machine
      basting, longarm frames, and individual providers may require different
      margins.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Check roll orientation</h2><p>
      A roll must cover one complete batting dimension without piecing. Use the <a
        href="/calculators/quilt-batting/">quilt batting calculator</a
      > to compare allowed orientations, or check <a
        href="/guides/how-much-extra-backing/">backing overage</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
